markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Conditionals</h1>
<p>Let's examine what's happening in the code from the previous level. When the painter reached that <code style="font-size:14px;">if</code> statement, it checked whether it could move south. If the path was clear, the painter moved and painted blue. If a truck was blocking the way, that condition failed and the painter skipped the action entirely.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
<p><b>📖 Conditional Statement:</b> A command that runs only if a certain condition is true, allowing a program to make decisions.</p>
</div>

<p>Let's walk through how this works, step by step.</p>

---

